    "#### Jaccard Similarity\n",
    "Jaccard similarity measures how much two sets overlap, and in text analysis, it’s often used to compare the unique words in two documents.\n",
    "$$ \\text{Jaccard similarity} = \\frac{A\\cap B}{A\\cup B}$$\n",
    "Where A and B are the sets of unique words from each text.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Interpretation**\n",
    "\n",
    "Range: The value ranges from 0 to 1.\n",
    "- 0 means the two texts share no words in common.\n",
    "- 1 means the two texts have exactly the same set of unique words.\n",
    "  \n",
    "Closer to 1: Higher overlap in vocabulary; the texts are more similar in terms of the words they use. \\\n",
    "Closer to 0: Little or no overlap; the texts are likely unrelated or discuss very different topics."
   ]
  },
