    "#### TF-IDF + Cosine Similarity\n",
    "\n",
    "TF-IDF + cosine similarity measures how similar two documents are by comparing the importance of each word (using TF-IDF weighting) and calculating the cosine of the angle between their vector representations.\n",
    "$$ \\text{Cosine similarity} = \\frac{A \\cdot B}{||A||\\text{ }||B||}$$\n",
    "where A and B are the TF-IDF vectors of the two documents.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Interpretation**\n",
    "\n",
    "Range: The value ranges from 0 to 1.\n",
    "- 0 means the documents have no similarity in their weighted word usage.\n",
    "- 1 means the documents are identical in their TF-IDF representation (i.e., they use the same words with the same importance).\n",
    "  \n",
    "Closer to 1: The documents share similar vocabulary and word importance, indicating high relatedness in content. \\\n",
    "Closer to 0: The documents are dissimilar in both word choice and importance, suggesting they discuss different topics or use different language."
   ]
